{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_w5ofx5yebdrljjtrahkyaqlwcorhbj7nihlow6cjpsocbo46qbmq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass, and I independently confirmed every claim on disk.\n\n## Result\n\n**The Rust translation is byte-for-byte faithful to the C. No divergence was found, so `src/lib.rs` needed no fixes.** The library is small (119 lines of C, two exported functions: `w_utf8_drop`, `w_utf8_filter`), so the work went into proving faithfulness rather than fixing bugs.\n\n## What was built\n\n**Phase A artifacts** (in `translation/`): `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md` (32 rows), `CONFIGS.md` (45 rows), plus `VERIFICATION.md` summarising results.\n\n**Tests** — every test dlopens *both* `.so` files via `libloading` and calls only exported C symbols (never Rust directly):\n- `tests/phase_b_configs.rs` — 45 tests, one per `CONFIGS.md` row (2000 seeded-random inputs per row; exhaustive sweeps of all 1-byte, all 65 025 2-byte, 23³/23⁴ boundary-byte, and all-256-second-bytes cases)\n- `tests/phase_c_errors.rs` — 34 tests, one per `ERRORS.md` row + an independent third-implementation oracle\n- `tests/fixtures/failalloc.c` — `LD_PRELOAD` allocator interposer for deterministic OOM injection *and* exact allocation tracing\n\n## Three checks that went beyond output comparison\n\n1. **Allocation-trace comparison.** `malloc_usable_size` turned out to be useless as an oracle (±16 bytes depending on chunk recycling), so instead the exact `malloc`/`realloc`/`strdup` request sequence is recorded and compared. This is what catches the odd `repl < 3` / `REPLACEMENT_INC` bookkeeping (a realloc on replacement #1, then every 1365th).\n2. **Guard-page row.** Input placed so its NUL is the last readable byte before a `PROT_NONE` page — proves neither side reads past the terminator.\n3. **`./mutation_check.sh`** injects 32 bugs one at a time; **all 32 detected, 0 survivors**. Two are content-*equivalent* (they only change which bytes are read) and are caught solely by the guard-page row; two only change allocation arithmetic and are caught solely by the trace rows.\n\n## Two issues I found and fixed in my own harness\n\n- The scratch dir leaked 46 517 files / 613 MB across runs.\n- **A real 1-in-8 flake**: the armed malloc failure was sometimes swallowed by a 48-byte Rust-runtime allocation, aborting the child. Fixed by gating injection on request size and adding a `fired` counter that every OOM row asserts. Confirmed stable over 8 consecutive suite runs + 3 full gate runs.\n\n## One documented deviation\n\n`assert()` passes `__FILE__`; the C's value is CMake's absolute build path (not reproducible), the Rust's is `c_src/src/lib.c`. The abort signal, assertion expression, line number (40/60) and function name are all asserted identical and mutation-tested.\n\nReproduce with `cd translation && ./check_all_features.sh && ./check_rows.sh && ./mutation_check.sh`. Note `.cargo/config.toml` sets `net.offline = true` — crates.io is unreachable here, so `libloading 0.8.9` came from the local registry cache."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":795,"cache_read_input_tokens":240006,"output_tokens":1172,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":795},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0cbdb97a-c3b3-44ac-914d-981e3e1a61b8","uuid":"811e8dc7-fd0d-41b6-a4b6-635b73dd399f","timestamp":"2026-08-27T20:35:54.167Z"}
